So if I put http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/341/intr-341.html#flying 
and http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/341/rint-341.html#levitation 
together I get the similarities and the differences in effects between 
the flying and levitation intrinsics.

Here follows my overview, made only out of my own interest.

+ means mostly positive effect
- means mostly negative effect

Effects with both flying and levitation:
+ Can pass over pits, holes, trap doors, squeaky boards, bear traps, 
water or lava safely. (Pits and holes in Sokoban will still trap you.)
+ Land mines have a chance of not being triggered, and will not wound 
your legs.
+ Improved chances of avoiding death by drawbridge.
+ Can move freely over ice or on the Plane of Air.
+ You are out of reach of xans' attacks.
+ You escape the dungeon rather than dying by level teleporting to 
levels between -9 and -1.

Only with flying:
+ Wounded legs do not reduce your carrying capacity.
+ No ill effects from descending stairs when encumbered, fumbling or 
punished.

Only with levitation:
+ Can move freely when fumbling.
+ Carrying capacity is at maximum.
+ Engravings will not be eroded by you.
+ When punished, iron balls will not drag you into traps they move onto.
- Cannot jump, set bear traps or land mines, dig downwards with an 
implement, sit, untrap traps, or spin webs.
- Cannot engrave other than with wands of magic missile, digging, fire, 
or lightning.
- Cannot pick up (except possibly by applying a bullwhip), feel, eat, 
sacrifice, loot, lock or unlock items on the floor.
- Cannot dip items into fountains or water.
- Cannot quaff from fountains or sinks.
- Cannot push boulders.
- Fragile items will usually break when dropped.
- Kicking requires wall, stone or door to brace against; doors cannot be 
kicked open.
- Kicking and throwing may lead to floating in opposite direction.
- Kicking tiny monsters may "miss wildly" and abuse dexterity.
- Cannot descend stairs or ladders.
- Cannot mount non-flying steeds unless levitating at will.

So it seems that flying is superior to levitation in general, though 
levitation still has some exclusive benefits.

Also (as a note to the spoiler maintainer) one negative effect of 
levitation apply to flying too, under certain circumstances: when flying 
is aquired by riding a creature and the rider is unskilled, the rider 
cannot pickup (etc?, not tested) things on the floor. But I guess this 
is better viewed as an effect of riding, and therefore better mentioned 
in the to-be-posted (news:40ab743d@news.comindico.com.au) Updated Riding 
Spoiler.

